0587.0, "source_doc_id": "52205", "income_statement_page": 2, "balance_sheet_page": 4, "cashflow_page": 7, "notes": "Hayleys Fibre PLC (coir/fibre products manufacturer, Hayleys Group, ~65% owned by Hayleys PLC). Clean single-rendering filing (no dual-extraction ambiguity). EPS cross-check: Group 98,768k/24,000,000 shares=4.115~=4.12 disclosed; Company 73,146k/24,000,000=3.048~=3.05 disclosed -- both tie, no column-swap issues. operating_profit = 'Results from operating activities'. This is the SECOND financial_statements entry for HEXP -- Q4 FY2025/26 (quarter ended 31 March 2026) was already stored (source_doc_id 51145), so this entry supports a genuine QoQ comparison in interim_updates in addition to YoY. Balance sheet compared against 31.03.2026 (Audited), the filing's own comparative column. short_term_borrowings = 'Current portion of interest bearing borrowings' + 'Short-term interest bearing borrowings'. long_term_borrowings = non-current 'Interest-bearing borrowings'. Cash flow IS disclosed on a standalone-quarter basis in this filing (unlike the prior Q4 FY2025/26 entry, where it was only cumulative and therefore left blank) -- capex = 'Purchase of property, plant and equipment'."}], "financials_annual": [], "market_data": {"symbol": "HEXP", "as_of": "2026-09-03", "collected_at": "2026-09-03T19:00:18.689348", "price": 172.75, "previous_close": 171.0, "closing_price": 172.75, "open": 173.0, "high": 175.0, "low": 169.0, "turnover": 17299429.25, "share_volume": 100310.0, "market_cap": 4146000000.0, "shares_outstanding": 24000000.0, "source": "tradeSummary", "valuation": null}, "thesis": null, "ratios": {"GROUP": []}, "report_diff": {"GROUP": []}, "interim_updates": [{"symbol": "HEXP", "company_name": "Hayleys Fibre PLC", "period_label": "Q1 FY2026/27 (quarter ended 30 June 2026)", "period_end_date": "2026-06-30", "generated_at": "2026-08-11T05:16:55.073163+00:00", "note_text": "Hayleys Fibre PLC's Group revenue grew 34% YoY to Rs.2,271.5mn for Q1 FY2026/27 (quarter ended 30 June 2026), with PAT up 40% to Rs.115.6mn (from Rs.82.7mn) and Results from Operating Activities up 46% to Rs.193.0mn. However, on a QoQ basis (vs Q4 FY2025/26, quarter ended 31 March 2026, already in this database), the picture is more mixed: revenue grew a further 24.3% sequentially (Rs.1,828.2mn to Rs.2,271.5mn), but Results from Operating Activities actually FELL 13.9% QoQ (Rs.224.2mn to Rs.193.0mn) and PBT fell 12.3% QoQ (Rs.184.4mn to Rs.161.7mn) -- margin compression despite higher volume. Selling and distribution expenses grew fastest of all cost lines YoY (+74%, Rs.35.7mn to Rs.62.1mn), well ahead of the 34% revenue growth, and net finance cost worsened both YoY (+39% to Rs.31.3mn) and structurally (short-term borrowings rose from Rs.1,849.3mn at 31 March 2026 to Rs.2,236.8mn at 30 June 2026, +21% in the quarter) as the Group funded a large working-capital build: trade and other receivables rose Rs.510.5mn and amounts due from related companies rose Rs.255.8mn during the quarter, pushing net cash used in operating activities to -Rs.377.1mn. At Company (standalone) level, the QoQ trend is the opposite of Group's: Company PBT grew 164.7% QoQ (Rs.39.5mn to Rs.104.5mn) and PAT grew 183.2% QoQ (Rs.25.8mn to Rs.73.1mn) -- meaning the sequential weakness sits specifically in HEXP's subsidiaries, not the parent.", "source_doc_id": "52205", "source_page": 2, "gaps_note": "QoQ comparison IS possible and included above (vs Q4 FY2025/26, quarter ended 31 March 2026, already stored in this database from a prior session) in addition to YoY. Cash flow this quarter is disclosed on a standalone basis (unlike the prior Q4 FY2025/26 entry, where cash flow was cumulative-only and left blank), so QoQ cash-flow comparison was not attempted despite both periods' PBT/operating figures being comparable.", "takeaway": "The YoY growth headline (+40% PAT) is real but masks a sequential QoQ deterioration at Group level (PBT -12.3%, operating profit -13.9%) driven by fast